meta {
  name: Member tags - Add a member
  type: http
  seq: 211
}

post {
  url: {{BASE_URL}}/api/v1/communities/nswswk8w8wso0ko8owwk8k0w/member-tags/<tag cuid>/members
  body: json
  auth: none
}

headers {
  Accept: application/json
  Content-Type: application/json
}

body:json {
  {
    "username": "ada-lovelace"
  }
}

docs {
  Puts the tag on a member of the community (#1389), named by exactly one of member (user cuid) or username; the owner counts as a member. Putting it twice changes nothing and answers 200. Someone who is not a member of the community gives a validation issue; an email field gives one too. A member has at most 20 tags in a community (422 after that). Nothing tells the member. Owner, admins, moderators with the manage members right, on any member, themselves too. Token ability: member-tags:write.
}
